# Data Policy — No Proactive Mock Data

## Rule

**Never add mock, test, placeholder, or example data to migrations, seed scripts, or any code that runs automatically.**

All application data is created by Phil through the app itself.

## What belongs in migrations (allowed)

Only rows the app **cannot function without**:

| What | Why it's allowed |
|---|---|
| `roles` rows (ADMIN, MEMBER, etc.) | RBAC is broken without them — auth would fail on first request |
| `permissions` rows | Same — `hasPermission()` would always return false |
| `role_permissions` join rows | Same — roles would have no permissions |
| Bootstrap admin account | One-time only, via `scripts/bootstrap-admin.ts`, skips if a user already exists |

## What does NOT belong in migrations (forbidden)

- Projects, units, project rows
- Team members or users beyond the bootstrap admin
- Lookup table rows (`scope_types`, `location_types`, `cost_types`, `install_teams`, `uom_types`, etc.)
- Any row whose purpose is to make the app "look populated" during development
- Anything described as "example", "placeholder", "sample", or "demo"

## If dev-only seed data is ever needed

Create `scripts/seed-dev.ts` — a standalone opt-in script Phil runs manually:
```bash
npm run seed:dev   # only if Phil explicitly asks for it
```
It must:
- Guard with `if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'development') throw ...`
- Never run as part of `dev:setup`, `db:migrate`, or any automatic pipeline
- Be clearly marked `DEV ONLY` at the top of the file

## Enforcement

Before writing any migration or seed script, ask: "Is this data required for the app to start and authenticate?" If no → it does not go in a migration.
